<title>SINGAPORE: SM SUMMIT SHARES PLUNGE FURTHER ON RUMOUR.</title>
<headline>SM SUMMIT SHARES PLUNGE FURTHER ON RUMOUR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in music disc maker SM Summit plunged more than 37 percent to a low of Singapore $0.66 on Wednesday amid rumours that the company was involved in a dispute with another firm.</p>
<p>Dealers said there were rumours of an argument with U.S. giant Microsoft Corp over the right to use certain software but were unclear on details.</p>
<p>Officials at SM Summit were unavailable for immediate comment.</p>
<p>SM Summit was last at S$0.73, down S$0.32.</p>
